  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.48–0.52) while image-only is weak (0.21), and scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 in singleprofile (0.520 vs 0.485). Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile aggregation improves upon the best singleprofile RNA result, and this is a key design axis before investing in multimodal fusion. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with simple average-pooling aggregation improve validation accuracy over the current best (config_004, scvi_n200 singleprofile, 0.520)? Why this is the best next experiment: It builds directly on our strongest encoder (scvi_n200), changes only the profile/aggregation axis (the minimal coupled change inherent to multiprofile), and uses the simplest aggregation (avgpool) to isolate whether multiple profiles add signal before introducing transformer complexity. A positive result justifies exploring transformer aggregation and multimodal extensions; a negative result tells us singleprofile suffices, redirecting budget toward encoder choice (scgpt) or multimodal fusion rather than aggregation architecture."
}

